sequenceDiagram
    participant Client1 as Client 1
    participant Client2 as Client 2
    participant StateMachine
    participant Database

    Note over Client1,Database: Concurrent Transition Scenario

    par Client 1 Transition
        Client1->>StateMachine: transition(payment1, PROCESSING)
        activate StateMachine
        StateMachine->>Database: SELECT payment
        Database-->>StateMachine: state: PENDING
    and Client 2 Transition
        Client2->>StateMachine: transition(payment1, FAILED)
        activate StateMachine
        StateMachine->>Database: SELECT payment
        Database-->>StateMachine: state: PENDING
    end

    Note over StateMachine,Database: Both validations pass

    par Atomic Database Operations
        StateMachine->>Database: transition_payment_state(PENDING → PROCESSING)
        activate Database
        Database->>Database: BEGIN TRANSACTION
        Database->>Database: CHECK current_state = PENDING
        Database->>Database: UPDATE state = PROCESSING
        Database->>Database: COMMIT
        deactivate Database
        Database-->>StateMachine: Success
        deactivate StateMachine
        StateMachine-->>Client1: Success
    and
        StateMachine->>Database: transition_payment_state(PENDING → FAILED)
        activate Database
        Database->>Database: BEGIN TRANSACTION
        Database->>Database: CHECK current_state = PENDING
        Note over Database: State already PROCESSING!
        Database->>Database: ROLLBACK
        deactivate Database
        Database-->>StateMachine: Error: State mismatch
        deactivate StateMachine
        StateMachine-->>Client2: StateTransitionError
    end

    Note over Client1,Client2: Only ONE transition succeeds<br/>Database atomicity prevents corruption
